From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 11:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Classify opaque clients by presentation geometry

The window rect may temporarily retain stale non-client frame extents while a
game removes its frame and switches to fullscreen.  Requiring that outer rect
to equal the client rect leaves the accelerated client below an opaque carrier
even when it covers the complete Wayland presentation surface.  The rendered
game then remains visible to workspace overviews but is hidden by the black
carrier in the normal workspace.

Use the visible presentation rect for this test.  This matches the existing
wayland_surface_client_fills_window() classification used by the dmabuf path
and retains all of the alpha, layered, shaped, GDI, and child-surface guards.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -2466,7 +2466,9 @@ static BOOL wayland_client_surface_should_stack_above_parent(
     if (content_over_producer || ReadAcquire(&client->has_alpha)) return FALSE;
     if (surface->window.exstyle & WS_EX_LAYERED) return FALSE;
     if (!wayland_surface_is_toplevel(surface) || surface->window.minimized) return FALSE;
-    if (!EqualRect(&surface->window.window_rect, &surface->window.client_rect)) return FALSE;
+    /* The outer Win32 rect may retain stale frame extents across a fullscreen
+     * transition; classify coverage against the Wayland presentation rect. */
+    if (!EqualRect(&surface->window.rect, &surface->window.client_rect)) return FALSE;
     if (surface->shaped) return FALSE;
     if (wayland_surface_dmabuf_stack_bottom(surface)) return FALSE;
     return TRUE;
